WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.462
- I look over and my roommate is

00:00:01.462 --> 00:00:03.079
on the phone with a tattoo shop.

00:00:03.079 --> 00:00:05.640
Am I really going to do this right now?

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:08.027
Let's go! We're Super Bowl champions baby!

00:00:09.827 --> 00:00:10.791
When I was a kid I never really thought

00:00:10.791 --> 00:00:13.414
I'd get a tattoo or do
anything that kind of crazy.

00:00:13.414 --> 00:00:15.016
My friends called me Caution Freak

00:00:15.016 --> 00:00:16.212
when I was growing up cause I wouldn't

00:00:16.212 --> 00:00:17.547
like skateboard or do anything.

00:00:17.547 --> 00:00:19.381
I was the kid with the camera
filming them doing everything.

00:00:19.381 --> 00:00:21.750
- The craziest thing I've
ever seen Brian do is

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:25.145
he bought a car after thinking
about it for eight months.

00:00:25.145 --> 00:00:26.080
- He's very responsible.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.691
He's the one that takes
the check to our landlord.

00:00:28.691 --> 00:00:31.141
You know, texting me at
ten o'clock at night like,

00:00:31.141 --> 00:00:32.801
"Hey are you gonna be home tonight?"

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:34.763
- Being from Colorado, I'm
a big Denver Broncos fan,

00:00:34.763 --> 00:00:36.562
and this year they made
it to the Super Bowl.

00:00:36.562 --> 00:00:39.020
- Brian was super pumped.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:40.952
- Oh I'm sorry, the Broncos
are winning ten to zero?

00:00:40.952 --> 00:00:42.019
Cam's got nothing right now.

00:00:42.019 --> 00:00:45.718
I'm starting to get just
really amped up about the game.

00:00:45.718 --> 00:00:48.483
(clapping)

00:00:48.483 --> 00:00:49.283
Let's go!

00:00:49.283 --> 00:00:50.192
Every time Denver does something great

00:00:50.192 --> 00:00:52.084
I'm like cheering, getting
into people's faces,

00:00:52.084 --> 00:00:53.560
being kind of annoying.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:54.580
(Brian shouting)

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.411
So I kind of started making
these bets saying like,

00:00:56.411 --> 00:00:58.248
- If Peyton Manning throws a pick

00:00:58.248 --> 00:00:59.588
you've got to take your shirt off.

00:00:59.588 --> 00:01:02.235
Yeah, there he is.

00:01:02.235 --> 00:01:03.941
Then I yelled, "Do the worm!"

00:01:03.941 --> 00:01:06.827
right after the Broncos
scored a touchdown.

00:01:06.827 --> 00:01:08.979
(people cheering)

00:01:08.979 --> 00:01:10.976
- I actually didn't even know
that I could do the worm.

00:01:10.976 --> 00:01:13.113
- We were like, "Buy us
pizza!" and he was like,

00:01:13.113 --> 00:01:14.413
- "I'll buy three large
pizzas for everyone to have."

00:01:14.413 --> 00:01:18.023
- Let's go Broncos!
(rhythmic clapping)

00:01:18.023 --> 00:01:19.706
- We were like, "Jump in
a pool!" and he was like,

00:01:19.706 --> 00:01:23.548
- Broncos! Broncos!
(people cheering)

00:01:23.548 --> 00:01:25.163
- And then we were just like,
"You know if the Broncos win,

00:01:25.163 --> 00:01:26.916
are you going to get a Super Bowl tattoo?

00:01:26.916 --> 00:01:28.169
You gotta get a Super Bowl tattoo."

00:01:28.169 --> 00:01:29.597
- And I was like, "Yeah sure."

00:01:29.597 --> 00:01:31.989
And then I look over and my roommate

00:01:31.989 --> 00:01:35.526
is on the phone with a
tattoo shop and I'm like,

00:01:35.526 --> 00:01:39.209
"Hm, am I really going
to do this right now?"

00:01:39.209 --> 00:01:41.275
Let's go! We're Super Bowl champions baby!

00:01:41.275 --> 00:01:44.005
(people cheering)

00:01:44.005 --> 00:01:46.436
(inaudible dialogue)

00:01:46.436 --> 00:01:50.596
(techno music)

00:01:50.596 --> 00:01:51.855
- [Man] Let's go Brian.

00:02:09.896 --> 00:02:12.867
- I didn't get the tattoo for
my friends, to appease them,

00:02:12.867 --> 00:02:14.121
and for everyone to cheer me on.

00:02:14.121 --> 00:02:16.408
It was really fun to just
go for something and do it,

00:02:16.408 --> 00:02:18.347
and in the moment just be like,

00:02:18.347 --> 00:02:20.595
"This is gonna happen no matter what."

00:02:20.595 --> 00:02:23.788
- In all honesty, it kind of
started making me think like,

00:02:23.788 --> 00:02:26.578
"Brian just got a tattoo,
and he just went for it."

00:02:26.578 --> 00:02:29.712
And as cliché as it might sound,
it started making me think,

00:02:29.712 --> 00:02:32.255
"What are things that
I should be going for

00:02:32.255 --> 00:02:34.835
and starting to just do with my life?"

00:02:34.835 --> 00:02:37.885
- Sometimes people are
too afraid to take a risk,

00:02:37.885 --> 00:02:40.718
whether it be a really
big thing or a small thing

00:02:40.718 --> 00:02:44.815
like getting a Super Bowl
tattoo, I think it's important.

00:02:44.815 --> 00:02:45.396
- I think the best part about

00:02:45.396 --> 00:02:47.358
getting a tattoo is it's a conversation.

00:02:47.358 --> 00:02:50.107
People will ask questions
about it, "What does it mean?"

00:02:50.107 --> 00:02:52.710
As simple as, "Oh, this
is when the Broncos

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:54.184
won the Super Bowl, Super Bowl 50."

00:02:54.184 --> 00:02:57.574
Or it's something deeper,
it has this meaning.

00:02:57.574 --> 00:03:00.047
But it's a conversation, it's
something that relates to you,

00:03:00.047 --> 00:03:02.151
and it's like a memory.

00:03:02.151 --> 00:03:04.330
My name is Brian, and I
got a Super Bowl tattoo.

